From: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] Count only Jupiter containers in the parameterized test

The outer JUnit 4 suite is launched through Vintage. Register Jupiter
explicitly in the nested launcher so the Vintage engine root does not
change the upstream fixture's Jupiter-specific container counts.

Upstream: downstream adaptation for running the JUnit 4 suite with Vintage
Reference: https://github.com/apache/maven-surefire/blob/surefire-3.5.5/surefire-providers/surefire-junit-platform/src/test/java/org/apache/maven/surefire/junitplatform/JUnitPlatformProviderTest.java
Signed-off-by: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
---
diff --git a/surefire-providers/surefire-junit-platform/src/test/java/org/apache/maven/surefire/junitplatform/JUnitPlatformProviderTest.java b/surefire-providers/surefire-junit-platform/src/test/java/org/apache/maven/surefire/junitplatform/JUnitPlatformProviderTest.java
--- a/surefire-providers/surefire-junit-platform/src/test/java/org/apache/maven/surefire/junitplatform/JUnitPlatformProviderTest.java
+++ b/surefire-providers/surefire-junit-platform/src/test/java/org/apache/maven/surefire/junitplatform/JUnitPlatformProviderTest.java
@@ -466,7 +466,9 @@
         adapter.setRunMode(NORMAL_RUN);
 
         JUnitPlatformProvider provider =
-                new JUnitPlatformProvider(parameters, createLauncherSessionWithListeners(executionListener, adapter));
+                new JUnitPlatformProvider(parameters, launcherSessionConfig(config -> config.enableTestEngineAutoRegistration(false)
+                                .addTestEngines(new org.junit.jupiter.engine.JupiterTestEngine())
+                                .addTestExecutionListeners(executionListener, adapter)));
 
         invokeProvider(provider, DisabledParameterizedTest.class);
 
